; error: 5:22: 'P' is a group of types, so a header writes it 'P...': a parameter's whole type, as in 'args: P...', or all a task's type takes, as in '(P...) -> R'; 'P' alone is one value's type, written only inside 'each v in args', as the type 'v' has
; `P` alone is the type of the value of a turn of `each v in args`, so it is
; written only inside one.
task last<P...: shown & fixed>(args: P...)
    hold kept: maybe P = none
    each v in args
        kept = v
    fi
    show(kept)
fi

task main()
    last(1, "two")
fi
